I have everything needed. Here is a thorough report of the current owner duplicate-detection code.

## Overview

The app is an OfficeFloor-based PetClinic. Owner creation flows through a single endpoint `POST /api/owners`, defined by a YAML pipeline. Duplicate detection is currently split across **three separate function classes** (telephone, email, household), each of which iterates `ownerRepository.findAll()`. There is **no** `identityKey` / `normalizedTelephone` field yet in `src/main` — those terms only appear as a *target* in the acceptance test comment. The refactor you're planning would consolidate these three checks into one derived `identityKey`.

---

## 1. Duplicate-detection functions

### `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/function/owner/EnsureUniqueTelephone.java`
Runs after Build, before Save. Iterates all owners, throws `DuplicateTelephoneException` on exact telephone match (telephone already normalized to E.164 by `BuildOwner`).
```java
public void service(@Val Owner owner, OwnerRepository ownerRepository) throws DuplicateTelephoneException {
    String telephone = owner.getTelephone();
    for (Owner existing : ownerRepository.findAll()) {
        if (telephone.equals(existing.getTelephone())) {
            throw new DuplicateTelephoneException(telephone);
        }
    }
}
```

### `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/function/owner/EnsureUniqueEmail.java`
Skips when email is null; otherwise exact-match on lower-cased email (lower-casing done in `Owner.setEmail`).
```java
public void service(@Val Owner owner, OwnerRepository ownerRepository) throws DuplicateEmailException {
    String email = owner.getEmail();
    if (email == null) { return; }
    for (Owner existing : ownerRepository.findAll()) {
        if (email.equals(existing.getEmail())) {
            throw new DuplicateEmailException(email);
        }
    }
}
```

### `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/function/owner/EnsureUniqueHousehold.java`
Skipped when `sharesHousehold == true`. Compares normalized (trim, collapse whitespace, lowercase) lastName + address. Note: its `normalize()` is a **local** lowercase normalizer, different from `AddressNormalizer` (which uppercases and expands abbreviations). The address stored on the owner has already been run through `AddressNormalizer` in `BuildOwner`, so this compares those uppercased values re-lowercased.
```java
public void service(@Val Owner owner, @Val Boolean sharesHousehold, OwnerRepository ownerRepository)
        throws DuplicateHouseholdException {
    if (Boolean.TRUE.equals(sharesHousehold)) { return; }
    String lastName = normalize(owner.getLastName());
    String address = normalize(owner.getAddress());
    for (Owner existing : ownerRepository.findAll()) {
        if (lastName.equals(normalize(existing.getLastName()))
                && address.equals(normalize(existing.getAddress()))) {
            throw new DuplicateHouseholdException(owner.getLastName(), owner.getAddress());
        }
    }
}
private static String normalize(String value) {
    return value == null ? "" : value.trim().replaceAll("\\s+", " ").toLowerCase();
}
```

### `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/function/owner/AssignHousehold.java`
Runs after the household uniqueness check when `sharesHousehold == true`. Derives a stable `HH-<12 hex>` id from SHA-256 of normalized lastName+address, sets it on the new owner, and back-fills existing same-household owners lacking an id. Full file worth seeing:
```java
public void service(@Val Owner owner, @Val Boolean sharesHousehold, OwnerRepository ownerRepository) {
    if (!Boolean.TRUE.equals(sharesHousehold)) { return; }
    String householdId = deriveId(owner.getLastName(), owner.getAddress());
    owner.setHouseholdId(householdId);
    for (Owner existing : ownerRepository.findAll()) {
        if (existing.getHouseholdId() == null && sameHousehold(owner, existing)) {
            existing.setHouseholdId(householdId);
            ownerRepository.save(existing);
        }
    }
}
// deriveId: key = normalize(last)+"|"+normalize(addr); SHA-256; "HH-" + first 6 bytes as %02X (12 hex chars)
// normalize(): trim, collapse whitespace, lowercase (same as EnsureUniqueHousehold)
```

### `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/function/owner/AddressNormalizer.java`
Canonical address form used in `BuildOwner` when storing the address: trim, collapse whitespace, **UPPERCASE**, expand `ST→STREET, RD→ROAD, AVE→AVENUE`. Blank → `""`. (Distinct from the lowercase `normalize()` helpers in the two household classes above — a subtlety to keep in mind when unifying into an `identityKey`.)

---

## 2. Owner entity — `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/model/Owner.java`

`@Entity @Table(name="owners")`, extends `Person` (firstName/lastName). Relevant columns/fields:
- `address` `@NotEmpty`
- `city` `@NotEmpty`
- `telephone` `@NotEmpty @Pattern("^\\+[0-9]{8,15}$", "E.164 form")`
- `email` — setter lower-cases: `this.email = email == null ? null : email.toLowerCase();`
- `registrationDate` (LocalDate)
- `customerCode` (String)
- `householdId` (String, column `household_id`)
- `namesakeCount` (Integer)
- `bulkSignupWarning` (Boolean)
- `pets` (`@OneToMany`, EAGER)

There is **no** `identityKey` / `normalizedTelephone` column yet.

---

## 3. Repository — `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/repository/OwnerRepository.java`

Interface methods available to the duplicate checks:
- `Collection<Owner> findByLastName(String lastName)`
- `Page<Owner> findByLastName(String lastName, Pageable)`
- `Owner findById(int id)`
- `void save(Owner owner)`
- `Collection<Owner> findAll()` ← used by all three duplicate checks
- `Page<Owner> findAll(Pageable)`
- `void delete(Owner owner)`

There is **no** finder by telephone/email/identityKey — duplicate detection currently relies on scanning `findAll()`. Implementations exist at:
- `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/repository/jpa/JpaOwnerRepositoryImpl.java`
- `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/repository/jdbc/JdbcOwnerRepositoryImpl.java`
- `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/repository/springdatajpa/SpringDataOwnerRepository.java`

(If you add an `identityKey` lookup you'll likely touch this interface plus these three impls.)

---

## 4. OfficeFloor REST + escalation YAMLs

### POST pipeline — `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/resources/officefloor/rest/api/owners.POST.yml`
`authorize: hasRole('OWNER_ADMIN')`. Full chain (each step `govern: [transaction]`, `next:` the following):
`build` (BuildOwner) → `ensureUnique` (EnsureUniqueTelephone) → `ensureUniqueEmail` (EnsureUniqueEmail) → `ensureUniqueHousehold` (EnsureUniqueHousehold) → `assignHousehold` (AssignHousehold) → `assignCode` (AssignCustomerCode) → `countNamesakes` (CountNamesakes) → `ensureCityCapacity` (EnsureCityCapacity) → `ensureDailyLimit` (EnsureDailyLimit) → `flagBulkSignup` (FlagBulkSignup) → `save` (SaveOwner) → `audit` (AuditOwnerCreated) → `respond` (RespondWithOwnerCreated).

To consolidate into one `identityKey` check you'd replace the three `ensureUnique*` steps here with a single step.

### Escalation registrations (dir `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/resources/officefloor/escalation/`)
Each maps an exception to its handler. Full contents:
- `org.springframework.samples.petclinic.rest.escalation.DuplicateTelephoneException.yml` → `handle.class: ...DuplicateTelephoneExceptionHandler`
- `...DuplicateEmailException.yml` → `...DuplicateEmailExceptionHandler`
- `...DuplicateHouseholdException.yml` → `...DuplicateHouseholdExceptionHandler`

Other escalation YAMLs present in that dir: `java.lang.Exception`, `DataIntegrityViolationException`, `CityAtCapacityException`, `DailyLimitExceededException`, `InvalidTelephoneException`, `NotFoundException`, `AuthorizationDeniedException`, `MethodArgumentNotValidException`.

### Exception + handler classes (all in `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/escalation/`)
Each exception extends `Exception` with a descriptive message; each handler builds a `ProblemDetail` via `ProblemDetails.build(ex, HttpStatus.CONFLICT, ex.getMessage())` and sends `ResponseEntity.status(CONFLICT).body(detail)`. Files:
- `DuplicateTelephoneException.java` — message `"Telephone already in use: " + telephone`
- `DuplicateTelephoneExceptionHandler.java` — returns **409 CONFLICT**
- `DuplicateEmailException.java` — `"Email already in use: " + email`
- `DuplicateEmailExceptionHandler.java` — **409**
- `DuplicateHouseholdException.java` — `"Household already registered: " + lastName + " at " + address`
- `DuplicateHouseholdExceptionHandler.java` — **409**

### `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/escalation/ProblemDetails.java`
Shared helper: `title` = exception simple name, `type` = `about:blank`, plus `timestamp` and empty `schemaValidationErrors` properties. All three 409 handlers use it.

---

## 5. Tests

### `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/test/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/acceptance/AcceptanceTest.java`
The single active duplicate test, whose class Javadoc names the target refactor: *"Consolidate all duplicate detection into a single derived 'identityKey' = normalizedTeleph..."*.
```java
@Test
void coreRejectsIdentityCollision() throws Exception {
    ObjectNode a = ownerNode();
    createOwnerOk(a);
    ObjectNode b = ownerNode();
    b.put("telephone", a.get("telephone").asText());
    createOwner(b).andExpect(status().isConflict()); // same identityKey
}
```

### `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/test/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/acceptance/AcceptanceBase.java`
Black-box base for `POST /api/owners`. `@SpringBootTest @AutoConfigureMockMvc @Transactional @WithMockUser(roles OWNER_ADMIN...)`. Key helpers: `ownerNode()` (fully-unique valid owner: firstName "Test", unique lastName/address/city/telephone, **no email**), `createOwner(body)` (POST), `createOwnerOk` (asserts 2xx + returns id), `createOwnerWithKey` (Idempotency-Key header), `getOwner`/`fetchOwner`, `uniqueTelephone()` = `04XXXXXXXX`. Also contains `sha256hex`/`shaHex`/`luhn` helpers that mirror the derivation algorithms (relevant if `identityKey` is SHA-derived). Note the comment at `deleteOwner`: soft-deleted records should be **ignored** by duplicate/identity checks (the current `findAll()` scans do not filter deleted records — a potential gap).

There is `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/test/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/acceptance/AuditLogCapture.java` (audit test support, not duplicate-specific).

---

## 6. Owner DTOs

The request/response types are **generated from OpenAPI** (`org.springframework.samples.petclinic.rest.dto.*`), not hand-written. The schema lives in `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/resources/openapi.yml`:

- **`OwnerFields`** (schema at lines 1991–2058) → generated `OwnerFieldsDto` — the **request** body used by `BuildOwner.service(@Valid @RequestBody OwnerFieldsDto ...)`. Fields: `firstName`, `lastName`, `address`, `city`, `telephone` (required set), plus optional `email`, `registrationDate`, and **`sharesHousehold`** (boolean; "When true, allow creating this owner even if another owner has the same last name and address" — this drives `EnsureUniqueHousehold`/`AssignHousehold`).
- **`Owner`** (schema at line 2059+, `allOf` OwnerFields + read-only props) → generated `OwnerDto` — the **response**. Read-only fields: `id`, `displayName`, `customerCode`, `membershipNumber`, `householdId` ("stable shared identifier for owners who share a household"), `namesakeCount`, `bulkSignupWarning`, `membershipLevel`, `initials`.

### `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/mapper/OwnerMapper.java`
MapStruct mapper. `toOwner(OwnerFieldsDto)` (ignores id + pets) builds the entity from the request; `toOwnerDto(Owner)` builds the response with derived expressions (displayName, membershipNumber, membershipLevel, locality, contactPreference). No duplicate logic here, but relevant since `sharesHousehold` on the DTO is read directly in `BuildOwner` (`request.getSharesHousehold()`), not via the mapper.

---

## Key takeaways for your refactor
- Three independent `findAll()`-scanning checks (`EnsureUniqueTelephone`, `EnsureUniqueEmail`, `EnsureUniqueHousehold`) each throw a distinct 409 exception. Consolidating into one derived `identityKey` means replacing steps `ensureUnique`, `ensureUniqueEmail`, `ensureUniqueHousehold` in `owners.POST.yml` with a single function, and deciding which exception/409 handler(s) to keep.
- No `identityKey`/`normalizedTelephone` field exists on `Owner` yet, nor any repository finder for it — both would be new.
- Normalization is inconsistent today: address is stored UPPERCASE (`AddressNormalizer`) but household comparison re-lowercases; telephone is E.164-normalized in `BuildOwner`; email is lowercased in `Owner.setEmail`. Any unified `identityKey` needs to pick canonical forms deliberately.
- The acceptance test comment explicitly states the intended target: `identityKey = normalizedTelephone` (truncated), and the only active duplicate test asserts a telephone collision returns 409.
- `AcceptanceBase.deleteOwner` documents that soft-deleted owners should be excluded from duplicate/identity checks — the current `findAll()` scans don't do this.

